<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edfu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Apollonopolis Magna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edfu is a town on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luxor">Luxor</a> and Aswan. It is known for its Temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horus">Horus</a>, built under the Ptolemies between 237 and 57 BCE and the best preserved temple of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, whose sanctuary holds a granite shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-ii">Nectanebo II</a>. Its walls carry long inscriptions on ritual, mythology and the geography of Egypt.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edfu.jpg" alt="Edfu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patrick.reb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Temple_Edfou_Egypte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
